ary constant $C$.\n\n$$\n\\int \\left(\\frac{6t^{2}+6}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Rewrite as powers, then apply the **sum and constant factor rules** and the power rule to each term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\left(\\frac{6t^{2}+6}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= \\int\\left(6t^{\\frac{3}{2}}+\\frac{6}{t^{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= 6\\int t^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t+6\\int t^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= 6\\left(\\frac{t^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{\\frac{5}{2}}\\right)+6\\left(\\frac{t^{\\frac{1}{2}}}{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)+C\\\\ &= \\frac{12t^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{5}+12t^{\\frac{1}{2}}+C\\\\ &= \\frac{12\\sqrt{t^{5}}}{5}+12\\sqrt{t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe arbitrary constants combine into one $C$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694471 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc494796-d3ff-50d3-857a-46e9faefb5e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{6\\sqrt{y^{5}}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc494796-d3ff-50d3-857a-46e9faefb5e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{6\\sqrt{y^{5}}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694475} :answer-field/id #uuid "e654dcda-12f6-562f-a498-d301818b5b0c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "90ccd6dd-b251-5d12-83e9-8fd73b918a03" :question/problem "For $y>0$, find the general antiderivative. Include the arbitrary constant $C$.\n\n$$\n\\int \\left(\\frac{3y^{2}-2}{\\sqrt{y}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Rewrite as powers, then apply the **sum and constant factor rules** and the power rule to each term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\left(\\frac{3y^{2}-2}{\\sqrt{y}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-\\frac{2}{y^{\\frac{1}{2}}}+3y^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= -2\\int y^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}y+3\\int y^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= -2\\left(\\frac{y^{\\frac{1}{2}}}{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)+3\\left(\\frac{y^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{\\frac{5}{2}}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -4y^{\\frac{1}{2}}+\\frac{6y^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{5}+C\\\\ &= -4\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{6\\sqrt{y^{5}}}{5}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe arbitrary constants combine into one $C$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694472 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c806a71-27e9-5e1b-b473-9a8ba5abf9dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10\\sqrt{y^{7}}}{7}-12\\sqrt{y}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c806a71-27e9-5e1b-b473-9a8ba5abf9dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10\\sqrt{y^{7}}}{7}-12\\sqrt{y}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694473} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f0540f0-d671-59c6-b7da-90699f93c074" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694465}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "95769440-0a3b-54ba-92a6-0e88c15d22a6" :question/problem "For $y>0$, find the general antiderivative. Include the arbitrary constant $C$.\n\n$$\n\\int \\left(\\frac{5y^{3}-6}{\\sqrt{y}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Rewrite as powers, then apply the **sum and constant factor rules** and the power rule to each term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\left(\\frac{5y^{3}-6}{\\sqrt{y}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= \\int\\left(5y^{\\frac{5}{2}}-\\frac{6}{y^{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= 5\\int y^{\\frac{5}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}y-6\\int y^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= 5\\left(\\frac{y^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{\\frac{7}{2}}\\right)-6\\left(\\frac{y^{\\frac{1}{2}}}{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)+C\\\\ &= \\frac{10y^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{7}-12y^{\\frac{1}{2}}+C\\\\ &= \\frac{10\\sqrt{y^{7}}}{7}-12\\sqrt{y}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe arbitrary constants combine into one $C$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694474 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce6e161b-8035-58fa-8ef9-525aa5000a83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\sqrt{t^{7}}}{7}-12\\sqrt{t}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce6e161b-8035-58fa-8ef9-525aa5000a83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\sqrt{t^{7}}}{7}-12\\sqrt{t}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694476} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f979cf0-e814-59c3-8ea9-2a33bcd0852e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ac0291d5-79fc-5f75-a8b1-e1418c1aba62" :question/problem "For $t>0$, find the general antiderivative. Include the arbitrary constant $C$.\n\n$$\n\\int \\left(\\frac{-2t^{3}-6}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Rewrite as powers, then apply the **sum and constant factor rules** and the power rule to each term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\left(\\frac{-2t^{3}-6}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-2t^{\\frac{5}{2}}-\\frac{6}{t^{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= -2\\int t^{\\frac{5}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t-6\\int t^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= -2\\left(\\frac{t^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{\\frac{7}{2}}\\right)-6\\left(\\frac{t^{\\frac{1}{2}}}{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{4t^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{7}-12t^{\\frac{1}{2}}+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{4\\sqrt{t^{7}}}{7}-12\\sqrt{t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe arbitrary constants combine into one $C$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694478 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74a4490d-7a39-5c15-9e07-952436729773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{t^{5}}}{5}-6\\sqrt{t}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74a4490d-7a39-5c15-9e07-952436729773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{t^{5}}}{5}-6\\sqrt{t}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694469} :answer-field/id #uuid "37bc5f34-d3f2-55ec-b5e2-270460534b94" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f96c992a-3e5a-54f0-a840-0746be4ecf81" :question/problem "For $t>0$, find the general antiderivative. Include the arbitrary constant $C$.\n\n$$\n\\int \\left(\\frac{-t^{2}-3}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Rewrite as powers, then apply the **sum and constant factor rules** and the power rule to each term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\left(\\frac{-t^{2}-3}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-t^{\\frac{3}{2}}-\\frac{3}{t^{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= -\\int t^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t-3\\int t^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= -\\left(\\frac{t^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{\\frac{5}{2}}\\right)-3\\left(\\frac{t^{\\frac{1}{2}}}{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{2t^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{5}-6t^{\\frac{1}{2}}+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{2\\sqrt{t^{5}}}{5}-6\\sqrt{t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe arbitrary constants combine into one $C$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694585 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dd3ca9a-2fa5-5646-8039-a52d1322d686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+\\frac{